body:
@beicause We use the parameter for static StringName variables, but we may have misunderstood the meaning of the parameter.

As I understand it, however, the issues we have don't seem to be related to our usage of the parameter but rather receiving static StringNames from interop and treating them as non-static. In other words, it doesn't seem we can check whether a StringName we received is static, and we may end up freeing it as a result.

But I think we now make a copy of every StringName we receive, so we should never be freeing the original StringName we received, and that may have fixed the issue. But I don't think the issue has been looked into recently.
